flowchart TD
A[Open surface] --> B{Content available?}
B -- no --> C[Show empty guidance]
B -- yes --> D[Review summary]
D --> E{Input valid?}
E -- no --> F[Show inline validation]
E -- yes --> G[Confirm action]
G --> H[Show progress]
H --> I{Completed?}
I -- yes --> J[Show updated state]
I -- no --> K[Show recoverable error]
K --> L[Retry or return]
Rationale: the flow documents the primary path and non-ideal states without implementation details.
Gate coverage: entry, decision, validation, confirmation, progress, success, failure, retry, cancellation, and return paths; consequential actions require explicit confirmation.
Path intent: repository/g/flows/core-flow.mmd; maintain one source flow per experience objective.
Writing rule: use plain verbs, explain outcomes, and avoid ambiguity, coercion, or preselected consequential choices.
Publishing rule: render the diagram, compare every branch with the state matrix, and record unresolved gaps before release.